      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Between August 1992 and July 1993, 27 patients aged 70 years of older with cholelithiasis were prospectively randomised into 2 groups. Fifteen patients underwent laparoscopic cholecystectomy and 12 patients underwent open cholecystectomy. Shorter operation time (93.3 +/- 25.3 minutes v. 176.3 +/- 26.1 minutes, P < 0.00001), fewer postoperative analgesic requirements (0.53 +/- 0.52 days v. 2.00 +/- 0.74 days, P < 0.00001), shorter postoperative hospital stay (3.93 +/- 1.71 days v. 7.92 +/- 0.79 days, P < 0.00001) and better cosmesis were found in the laparoscopic cholecystectomy group. The above data suggest that laparoscopic cholecystectomy is the treatment of choice for cholecystolithiasis in elderly patients."},
